    "description": "Write eval baselines at two repeats\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR records two eval decisions in the docs. It changes no code.\n\n- A new baseline is written at two repeats, not three. Two repeats give the spread that the margin rule needs, at less cost.\n- A routine eval against the baseline stays at one repeat.\n- To cut noise, the case set grows before the repeat count does. More cases reduce the noise of one case and the noise between runs. More repeats reduce only the noise between runs. In the D7 evals, one case moved precision by 0.1 between two runs of nearly the same code.\n\nThe README baseline section, design section 8 and the D4b ticket now say this. The CI eval job keeps `--repeat 3`, because a change to it is a workflow change.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test` passes.\n- [x] `scripts/check-version-bump.sh` says the change touches no shipped file.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XrBTZfeb8Fxs7Pynw8RhjV\n",
